  "plain": "James Fox, a filmmaker who investigates UFOs, says he looked into a case from 1996 in Varginha, a town in Brazil, where a UFO is said to have crashed and a being was reportedly captured. Fox says he travelled there five times over twelve years, and the work went into his film Moment of Contact. The journalist Michael Shellenberger later wrote about the case in a two-page spread in the New York Post newspaper, and the host Jesse Michels points to Fox's work there too, since if true it would be a crash with living non-human beings."
